#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:17
msgid "11. Bluetooth Lock Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:26
msgid "A servo motor stands in for the bolt of a lock. One character from the phone turns it: ``1`` locks, ``0`` unlocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:29
msgid "Two states are enough for a lock, so the sketch needs no message terminator - every single character that arrives is a complete command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:34
msgid "1. Build the Circuit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:38
msgid "The module draws a high current at start-up, so make sure the 9 V battery or an external power supply is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima. A servo has its own current spike - never feed it from the 5 V pin of the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:44
msgid ":ref:`cpn_uno`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:45
msgid ":ref:`cpn_espc201`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:46
msgid ":ref:`cpn_servo`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:50
msgid "2. Upload the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:52
msgid "Open the ``11-Bluetooth_lock_controller.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\bluetooth\\11-Bluetooth_lock_controller``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:55
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:57
msgid "The Serial Monitor at **115200** shows the two Bluetooth lines, and then one line for every command you send:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:70
msgid "3. Lock and Unlock from the Phone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:72
msgid "Open LightBlue, tap **Scan** and connect to **SunFounder-C2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:74
msgid "Expand the service **0xA002** and open the characteristic **C304**. Then tap **Write new value**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:79
msgid "Set the format in the top right corner to **UTF-8 String** and type ``1``. The picture shows the field just before sending:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:84
msgid "Send it. The servo turns to the locked position and the Serial Monitor prints ``Locked``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:87
msgid "Type ``0`` in the same field and send it - the servo swings back and the monitor prints ``Unlocked``. The picture shows the field again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:95
msgid "The servo angles are ``lockAngle`` and ``unlockAngle`` at the top of the sketch. If your lock mechanism moves the wrong way, swap the two numbers instead of turning the horn by hand - that is easier to undo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:101
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:103
msgid "**The servo**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:113
msgid "``myservo.write(angle)`` moves the horn to a position between 0 and 180 degrees and holds it there. It does not spin continuously - which is exactly what a lock bolt needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:116
msgid "**Waiting for one character**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:132
msgid "``bleSerial.read()`` returns **one** character, which is why the phone must send ``1`` and not ``Lock``. Anything that is not ``1`` or ``0`` is ignored without complaint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:137
msgid "``'1'`` with single quotes is a character; ``\"1\"`` with double quotes is a text of one character and the comparison would not compile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:140
msgid "**Why no terminator is needed**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/11-iot_Bluetooth_lock_controller.rst:142
msgid "Every command here is exactly one character long, so the sketch cannot get out of step. In the piano and OLED projects the messages are longer, and there a terminator is required - look for ``*`` and ``#`` in the next chapters."
msgstr ""
